+    "debriefMsg": "\nPremedicate to prevent tachycardia.  Use routine monitoring plus direct arterial pressure. Consider PA catheter for LV filling pressure and SVR. However, there is an increased risk of arrhythmias with PA catheter.  Administer fluid bolus to restore intravascular volume.  Preoxygenate, induce anesthesia with minimum dose of etomidate, administer relaxant, and intubate. Maintain anesthesia with a moderate amount of narcotics, with roughly half MAC potent inhalation agent as tolerated. Maintain adequate preload.  Keep heart rate down and SVR up - use phenylephrine as needed. Treat hypotension immediately.\n\n", 
