+    "title": "Case 14 - 54 year old with cor pulmonale for emergency laparotomy", 
+    "badDrugs": ["Dantrolene"], 
+    "coMin": 1, 
+    "debriefMsg": "\n\nYou must become adept at the differential diagnosis of hypotension under anesthesia. Think: (1) Preload, (2) Pump, (3) Afterload.  In this case it is the pump - the right ventricle is unable to pump adequately against the exceedingly high pulmonary vascular resistance. Maintain appropriate ventilation.  Avoid hypoventilation which will raise pulmonary vascular resistance and worsen right-sided failure. Also, avoid hyperventilation which will cause hypokalemia. \n\n", 
+    "depthCarina": 25, 
+    "depthCords": 18, 
+    "depthTubeInitial": 22, 
