+    "preopMsg": "\n54 year old with cor pulmonale for emergency laparotomy\n\nHistory of Present Illness\nPatient has actively bleeding ulcer; transfused 10 units in the last 12 hours.\n\n\nPast Medical History\nIllnesses: Severe chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. Fatigue, dyspnea on exertion walking one block, short of breath with conversation, uses home oxygen. Recurrent pneumonias. Required mechanical ventilation for one week last year.\nSurgeries: Lumbar laminectomy (GA) with no complications 10 years ago.\nMeds: digoxin, lasix, albuterol, ipratropium, omeprazole\nNo known drug allergies\nHabits: Quit smoking 1 year ago, denies alcohol\n\nFamily History\nNo anesthetic complications\n\nPhysical Exam\nModerately obese male, short of breath, in moderate pain\nWeight: 82 kg    HR: 98     BP: 124/78    RR: 18\nAirway: normal\nLungs: distant breath sounds, uses accessory muscles\nHeart: S3, jugular venous distension, hepatomegaly, peripheral edema\n\nLabs\nHct: 48;   Lytes, Glucose, Bun, Cr: normal\nRoom air ABG: pH: 7.35, pCO2: 46, pO2: 54\nECG: sinus rhythm, right atrial and ventricular hypertrophy\nCXR: right ventricular hypertrophy, prominent pulmonary artery\n\nNPO Status\nLast ate 16 hours ago. \n\nPatient and Surgeon Requests\nSurgery is scheduled for 3 hours.\n\n\n", 
