+    "coMin": 1, 
+    "debriefMsg": "You must become adept at the differential diagnosis of hypertension under anesthesia. Thyrotoxicosis is relatively uncommon but should be suspected if a patient with thyroid disease. \n\nControl the tachycardia with beta-blockade. Administer cold crystalloid with glucose. In addition, administer sodium iodide, cortisol, and propylthiouracil. Avoid aspirin.\n\n", 
+    "depthCarina": 25, 
